## 12. Intellectual Property and Code Ownership

### 12.1 Company Ownership

All work created by employees during employment is owned by BrightPath, including:
- Source code and software developed
- Documentation and technical writing
- Product designs and specifications
- Marketing materials and content
- Tools and utilities created for company use

### 12.2 Open Source and Third-Party Code

**Approved Use:**
- Open-source libraries and frameworks are permitted for company projects
- License compliance is required (GPL, MIT, Apache, etc. have different rules)
- IT maintains a list of approved open-source libraries

**Prohibited:**
- Copying code from competitors' products
- Using third-party code without appropriate license attribution
- Violating GPL requirements (requiring code to be open source)

### 12.3 Personal Projects

- Work on personal projects using company equipment or time is prohibited
- Personal projects developed after hours on personal equipment are generally employee-owned (not company property)
- If a personal project relates to company business or uses company knowledge, it may be company property (discuss with manager)

