## 16. Violations and Consequences

### 16.1 Policy Violations

Examples of violations:
- Disclosing confidential information to unauthorized persons
- Unauthorized access to confidential systems or data
- Sharing passwords or disabling security controls
- Misusing company devices or systems
- Failing to report suspected security incidents
- Violating customer data protection agreements
- Downloading or accessing prohibited content on company devices

### 16.2 Disciplinary Action

**Consequences depend on severity:**

| Violation | Severity | Action |
|-----------|----------|--------|
| Phishing click (first time) | Low | Training/coaching |
| Failing to lock device | Low–Medium | Reminder, escalation if repeated |
| Sharing password with colleague | Medium | Written warning, retraining |
| Downloading confidential data without authorization | High | Suspension, possible termination |
| Intentional data theft or sale | Critical | Immediate termination + legal action |

### 16.3 Legal Consequences

Serious violations may result in:
- Criminal prosecution for data theft
- Civil lawsuits for damages
- Enforcement of non-compete and non-disclosure agreements
- Restraining orders preventing disclosure

