## 17. Frequently Asked Questions

**Q: Can I take a photo of my screen to share with a colleague?**  
A: Avoid screenshots if the screen contains confidential information. If necessary, redact sensitive details before sharing. Better: Use a secure file transfer or direct system access rather than screenshots.

**Q: Is it okay to work on a customer case on my personal laptop at home?**  
A: Only if you have written approval for remote work and your personal device has full-disk encryption and VPN access. Company data should not be on unencrypted personal devices.

**Q: I accidentally sent customer data to the wrong email address. What should I do?**  
A: Report immediately to IT security@brightpath.com. Do not attempt to "unsend." IT will contact the recipient and take steps to retrieve or quarantine the email.

**Q: Can I discuss BrightPath strategy in a closed LinkedIn discussion group?**  
A: No. LinkedIn discussions, even "private" groups, are not confidential. Do not disclose strategic or confidential information on any social platform.

**Q: What happens if I find a confidential document left on a printer or in a meeting room?**  
A: Secure the document, do not read it if it's not relevant to you, and return it to the owner or HR. Report the incident to your manager to prevent future occurrences.

**Q: Can I give my password to IT support if they ask for it to troubleshoot my account?**  
A: No. IT should never ask for your password. Legitimate IT support resets passwords or uses administrative access without needing your password. If this request is made, report it as a suspected phishing/social engineering attempt.

